  "extraction_notes": "Figure 1 shows a generic direct amidation reaction between a carboxylic acid and an amine catalyzed by various boronic acids (1-6). The reaction is split into two groups based on the required temperature. Entry 'header' represents the generic scope transformation. Entries '1'-'6' represent specific catalysts used for this transformation with their respective temperature ranges. Catalyst 3 is a pyridinium salt; only the cation is provided in the SMILES. Catalyst 2 has a diisopropylaminomethyl group ortho to the boronic acid and a trifluoromethyl group para to it. Catalyst 6 is 2-iodo-5-methoxyphenylboronic acid."
}